                        Introduction to LogicBBS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


 LogicBBS is a host bulletin board system, and with this software you will
 be able to transfer data using a modem. This software is only a host program.
 People calling your BBS will need a terminal program. You should be familiar
 with at least one of the following programs; Jr-Comm,Terminus,N-comm,Term.
 With one these programs users will be able to call up LogicBBS and transfer
 data between LogicBBS and their terminal.

 LogicBBS is based on the workings and design of another bbs software system
 called Ami-Express. In other words the main idea was to create a bbs system
 that was easy to install and also with alot of useful features for sysops.
 As we only had good experiences calling Amix systems it is obvious that the
 first versions of LogicBBS looks and acts alot like Amix. But LogicBBS is in
 no way based upon the source for Amix or for that matter any other BBS source.
 And when you get more familiar with LBBS you should notice alot of features
 which are not related to any one system. This BBS was 100% made in assembly
 language.

 Former Ami-Express owners may find commands and setup similar, but alot of
 new features have also been included in LogicBBS.
 It is also possible to run Ami-Express doors and rexx scripts. But the native
 LogicBBS doors and rexx scripts are much more powerful and should be easier
 and give better execution speed. The full range of Ami-Express is not support
 only the most common. And the data files are not in any way identical to
 LogicBBS.
